{
  "name": "bfcpu",
  "description": "A hardware implementation of a CPU architecture based on the Brainfuck ISA, utilizing an AVR-based microcontroller as a bridge. The system implements a custom SPI protocol to facilitate I/O between the CPU core and a USB UART interface, managing bi-directional data flow through master/slave role switching. It provides a low-level hardware abstraction layer for serial communication and peripheral control on Atmel AVR platforms.",
